outcome pairs of (outcome in A minus outcome in B). That sum is 6000. So the reason prefers the lottery with the more favorable sum of outcome differences. Since this sum is positive and only applies to A, the reason would prefer A. But the individual chose B. So the reason as defined would prefer A, not B. Therefore, the decision reason is applicable and can be evaluated.",
