n compares the sum of differences between outcomes. In this case, the sum of differences (A’s outcomes minus B’s outcome) is (3000 - 2000) + (-3000 - 2000) = 1000 - 5000 = -4000. The sum for B (if we consider only one outcome) is 0 (no differences). So B has a more favorable sum (0 > -4000). Therefore, the decision reason would prefer B. The information relevant to the decision reason is thus derived and clearly defined: the sum of pairwise differences of outcomes is -4000 for A and 0 for B (by default), so B is preferred by the reason.",
